
==========================================================================
RELEASE NOTES for MAX 4.2.10, MCC 2.1.0 SUE/DPC 4.3.5  (mmi_011231)
==========================================================================

---------
 GENERAL
---------

All manuals and tutorials have been updated.


----------------------
 MAX and MAX-LS 4.2.10
----------------------

Enhancements since MAX 4.0.2
----------------------------

Significant memory improvements (generally 2X less memory)

Performance improvements

Added "check connectivity" option to wire tool. If set, the wire tool
will give a warning if you are connecting two texted nets with different
names.

Enhanced cross-probing between MAX and SUE.  You now can have multiple
SUE and MAX sessions running.  Also, you can now specify the technology
to use if starting a new MAX for running the layout generator.

File menu change: "Save and descendents" changed to "Save Multiple" with
a sub-menu for "save all modified cell buffers".

Added performance warning for "flylines follow mouse" option in wire tool.

One button Calibre run from DRC Setup menu.

Improved MAX DRC and Calibre DRC interface.

Added ability to edit non-manhattan polygon edges.

Performance improvements when flattening cells.

"See Mask" menu becomes multi-column if too many layers.

Box mode: Changed so that button-1 either creates or resizes box 
depending on where you start.

Modified Shift-But-1 to just create a box.

File select box now shows if a file is a link

Added "Toggle Read-only" to the File menu.

"Dog-bone" fets can now be created with the fet gcell.

Improvements to "Select Cell by Name".

You can now select multiple nets with the "Select Net (add)" option.

Select net by name feature added including pattern matching to 
highlight nets.

Select net for large nets (i.e. VDD,GND,Clk) asks if you want to continue

If no wiring layer under cursor, select net will now trace connectivity
of any layer under the cursor.

Changes to make_tech:
     1. Removed squaring of vias by default in make_tech.  Instead only square
     if the line 

        square_vias

     is present in the tech source file.

     2. If you want to specify how to netlist (using :extract) the bulk
     terminal of a fet, you can now do it with make_tech.
     The new syntax is:

         device nfet from poly ndif -bulk_terminal <bulk_name>

Fixed bug in selecting nets with close non-manhattan polygons.

Max redisplay bug fixed.

Max bug where paint was left in select group fixed.

license bug fix: tools now check the MMI_LICENSE_FILE variable.

bug fix: grid offset now works

BETA release for the HP platform (GDSPLOT interface not included).


Known Bugs
----------
In order to get crossprobing to work properly, you need to 
first do a "MAX Crossprobe Init" from SUE.  If you only
do a "SUE Crossprobe Init" from MAX, then you won't be able
to "Crossprobe Net".  

There is a Max performance bug in true-color (aka 16-bit) mode
for some Xserver/driver combinations.  If Max graphics is painfully
slow, and you can actually observe the window being drawn from
top to bottom (even when zoomed in tight) - you have this problem.
The work-around is to change your Xserver to 8-bit (pseudo-color) mode.



-----------------
SUE/DPC/NST 4.3.5
-----------------

Enhancements since SUE/DPC 4.2.7
--------------------------------

Added congestion analysis to DPC.  DPC will now compute and
display the congestion from DPC on the placement view.  Click
on "Help" in the popup form when you select "Sim->Congestion"
for more details on congestion analysis.  The feature is
currently only a beta release.

Uses a new netlist database and parser.
	- Significant performance improvements.
	- Cell, instance and net names must now
	  use valid Verilog syntax.

New DPC feature "Display Connections" in the placement view
which displays the connections with flylines to the selected
instances.

Added ability to place top-level pins in DPC (automatic pin placement).
Inputs/outputs/inputs are aligned to connections in placement
and are added to side corresponding to their orientation in
the schematic.  To enable use: set DPC(PINS) 1.  Pins are
shown in placement view, CP includes pins and estimated
parasitics include pin locations.

Can add a "halo" around the placement view for extra routing
room.  Especially useful with pins to give the router room
to route to.  Visible in DPC placement.  To enable use:
	SET DPC(HALO) <grids_of_halo>
Defaults to 0.

Added DPC(LEF_PATH) which contains a list of paths to LEF leaf
cell definitions.  Not required.  Wildcarding allowed.  If
present, overrides DPC(PATH).  So, DPC can now get the cell
sizes directly from the LEF files. 

Improved primetime interface to work with newest primetime
bug fixes (2000.11 release).  It is suggested that you 
run with "set DPC(MIN_RC) 0ps"

In DPC_TIMING(ctlf_file), If a path name includes "ctlf" in the
name (or extension), uses readctlf in Pearl, otherwise uses readtlf.

Added ability to rotate leaf cells with ports files and a
specified orientation.  Add R90 (case sensitive) to the dpc
property to rotate 90 degrees.  Use R90 with mirror and flip 
to get all orientations.

Changed display design hierarchy to query the user if in a
schematic that is not in the current netlist hierarchy.  User
can make current the new top level or switch to existing
neltist hierarchy.

Added a ruler command.  Mainly for DPC placements.
	- Added a ruler setup command to change ruler parameters.
	  New ruler parameter to toggle default ruler mode of
	  either manhattan or diagonal.

Show selected terms now works on hierarchical placement cells.  Also
shows pin direction.

Moved parasitic creation to time_it so DPC Netlist doesn't
do the parasitic creation.  Note: time_it won't redo
parasitics unless it has to.  DPC_it does DPC Netlist followed
by time_it.

Enhanced row position control for DPC.

Added an option to Select Simulator menu in spice mode to
specify the output data suffix.  For spice this defaults to
.tr0 with the SPICE_SUFFIX(spice) variable but if running an
ac simulation you want to change this to .ac0.

Now ignores duplicate property definitions in icons.

Added last modified by to title bars.

Added a new "name_net" called a suggested_name.  It is part of
the "name_net_s" generator -- i.e. just shift-double-click on
a name_net and you will see it.  A suggested_name on a net
will only name the net if nothing else names it -- i.e. it has
a lower priority than either globals, I/O's or name_nets.
Furthermore, unlike a name_net, nets with the same suggested
name will NOT get tied together.  Instead, one of the nets
will get a unique name.  The suggested names were added so
that you can have unnamed nets whose name doesn't change with
each netlisting.  To facilitate this, there is a new global
variable called CREATE_SUGGESTED_NAMES which defaults to false
(0) but when set to true (1) will added suggested_name icons
to all unnamed nets after netlisting (technically after
generating term names).  

Changed "Edit Selected" to "Edit Properties..." to better explain
function and make in line with MAX.

Added Control-Button-1 in schematics list box to drop the
corresponding icon into the current schematic.

Added NETLIST(ignore_connected_outputs) to ignore errors if
outputs are tied together. 

Added more font sizes in SUE.  There are now 5 sizes.

Options to starting sue are now case insensitive.  For
example, can now do: "sue -set foo=3" or "sue -SET foo=3"

Prompt, title, and icon name are now synchoronized visually
for multiple sue sessions.  The second simultaneous sue
session is called SUE#2, etc.

Comma-delimited signals are now handled properly by
sue2edif and edif2sue.

A scalar signal into a bused input is now duplicated in verilog as was
done in spice.  Bug fix.

Added tcl coding example in $MMI_TOOLS/mmi_local.sample/sue

Fixes to edif2sue and sue2edif.

IRSIM now works.  There are some interem version of SUE in which 
IRSIM was not compiled correctly.

---------
MCC 2.1.0
---------

Enhancements since MCC 2.0.5
----------------------------

        Implemented creation of a layout of the critical path as
        agreed upon.  To use, select layout as the option in
        MCC critical path.

        There are some new switches to control the critical path
        generation:

                # set CP_TIE_INPUT(<cell_type>,<port>) <signal>
                # set CP_TIE_INPUT(DEFAULT) <signal>

                # for example,
                # set CP_TIE_INPUT(sram_cell,wl) gnd
                # set CP_TIE_INPUT(sram_cell,bl) vdd
                # set CP_TIE_INPUT(sram_cell,bl_L) vdd
                # set CP_TIE_INPUT(DEFAULT) gnd

        To tie off inputs in the layout with text.

                set CP_TRACE_BASIC 0 or 1

        If set to 0, like the old way.  If 1, only traces the
        outputs of receivers, not the drivers.  Will create a
        smaller critical path circuit.

        Also implemented an option to include the wires in a halo
        around the critical path wire for better extraction.

                set CP_HALO 1 or 0

        CP_HALO = 1 turns feature on.

        Use CP_HALO_RADIUS to specify how far the halo extends (in microns)

                set CP_HALO_RADIUS <microns_of_extent>




============================================================================
RELEASE NOTES for MAX 4.0.2, MCC 2.0.5 SUE 4.2.7 and DPC 4.2.7  (mmi_001220)
============================================================================

There have been many enhancements added to MAX, SUE and DPC since the 
last release (mmi_000427).  This file lists the enhancements, known limitations
and know bugs for the mmi_001220 release.  Not every enhancement is
listed, so please refer to the user manual for more information. 

===============
***IMPORTANT***
===============

IF YOU HAVE OLDER VERSIONS OF MAX:

If you read in a MAX file into the new 4.0.2 version of MAX, the will not
be readable by older versions of MAX.  You would have to write out a
GDSII file from MAX 4.0.2 and read the GDSII file into the older version
of MAX.

To have access to Calibre DRC from the Tool menu, you need to update your
$MMI_TOOLS/../mmi_local/max/.maxrc with the info in the 
$MMI_TOOLS/mmi_local.sample/max/.maxrc file for this release.

Tcl files in the $MMI_TOOLS/../mmi_local/max directory may be incompatible
with the new version of max.  Support for extraction, lvs and calibre
are now included inside max.  Any .tcl files for these purposes
located in your $MMI_TOOLS/../mmi_local/max directory should be removed.

Your best bet is to replace the entire contents of your
$MMI_TOOLS/../mmi_local/max directory with the new
$MMI_TOOLS/mmi_local.sample/max directory provided in this release.


