----------------
 MAX and MAX-LS
----------------

Enhancements since MAX 3.2.14
-----------------------------

Industrial Strength
-------------------

More Layers allowed for a MAX technology - over 100 layers

Larger coordinates allowed 

A number of big-design performance improvements

New Features
------------

Added True Color Graphics Capability (no longer a limition of 8-bit
graphics mode)

Added Groups - container for arbitrary layout.
Groups are persistent (saved in max file) and editable.

Support for Artwork Conversion's GDSPLOT - Included for free with
every copy of MAX.

Added "Align" command.

Added "Display Cell Doc..." command.

Added "Probe" command to show what layers/cells are under a specific point.

User programmable hot-keys.  

Mentor Graphics' Calibre DRC support built in.

New DRC feedback window - makes it easier to see both MAX internal
and Calibire DRC feedback.

Fet gcell: Added support for dog-bone fets, added support for partially 
contacted fets.

Via gcell: Added support support for assymetric vias, added support for 
minimum size vias even if center would be off grid; it is moved on-grid.

Added warp cursor - user convenience to place cursor over opened menu.

Added Edit Cell Properties - can now specify the instance name

Added "Zoom in" option and wild cards to select net by name.

Added array pop-up form

Select net command (hotkey: s) now cycles through layers under cursor


Redisplay
---------

Multiple highlight colors support (e.g. box vs selection)

More control of displayed text size for labels.

Dimming labels, text and flylines and bbox outlines in non-editcell 
(previously only paint).

GDS
---

Implemented snap-to arbitrary grid on GDSII input.

GDSII write now defaults to flattening gcells (which is usually what
is wanted.)

Import/Export File now in File menu, includes GDS import/export
and "Create tech file from GDS file".  Many new GDS import/export options.



Platforms and Licensing
-----------------------

Executables now work for Red Hat 6 or 7 systems, but no longer for Red Hat 5
systems. 

Update to FlexLM version 7.1, support for ~/.flexlmrc file.  FlexLM licensing
now works for Solaris 7 and 8 machines.

If license server dies, now prints warning message - don't lose any work


Other Enhancements
------------------

GCell information saved in .max file.  If the Gcell tcl definition
changes, the Gcell will be read in with the old information.

Interactive DRC enhancement: asymetric via enclosure checks

Can now drag cells over exact copies without one disappearing.

If you type, "max foo.", MAX now trys to load the file "foo.max" 

Added "Generate Layers" command to auto-generate nplus/pplus/well.

New key bindings for some commands which are more consistent with SUE.
Note: use legacy.keymap for old keymap.

Added "Move cell origin" command, and several other move methods 
(Move To, Move To Point, Move to Box)

The rotate/flip commands align new cell origin to grid if there is just 
one cell and the original cell origin was on grid.

Added "Save As..." command.

Added Manufacturing Mask grid and programmable symmetric or assymetric user 
defined grid.  All max user commands snap to the new user grid.
New hot-keys let users switch grids rapidly with 1, 2, 3, 4 keys.

Added flatten setup menu, flatten one-level or hierarchy option,
flatten only text command, and flatten to group.

User visible tcl functions:  prop_dialog; new options to prop_menu;
better techinfo documentation.

Button-1 select now selects wire segment, not just largest piece of paint.

Wire tool draws 45 wires in foundry approved manner:
Now uses wire-paths for horizontal segments adjacent to 45 segments.

Clipboard cut/paste now works between MAX sessions.

Gcell directory moved from <path>/max/gcells to <path>/max/cells; 
this directory can now contain any cells, not just gcells.

Start-up file can now use either max.rc or .maxrc (but not both 
in the same directory.)

Add "unconnected label" warning to select net by name

Added message to area select that indicates what, if anything, selected.

Made undo/redo not switch cells without asking.

Allow user to redefine their own gcells.
Add message if user tries to define the same gcell twice.

Layout Generator:
For shared diffusion, check if flipping fets will reduce capacitance.
Add ability to draw gcells with missing contacts, and always use gcells by default.
Added flyline_crossing_minimization option to layout generator,
Make vdd/gnd names programmable in stdcell generator.

Added asymetric wire snap (separate X and Y snap grids).

Print warning if entered wire width is less than tech file width;
it goes ahead and uses the tech file width.

Wire tool:
Can now change via drag mode "c" before dropping via.
Added "r" hotkey to rotate vias, "x" for assymetric vias.
Now allow arguments to gcell via name



Bug Fix Highlights
------------------

Fixed drc (hier processing) bug.

Fixed netlisting (and simple extraction).

Fixed intermittent wrong bounding box problem.

Fixed several redisplay glitches.

(Numerous other bug fixes.)


Discontinued Features
---------------------

Fancy extractor features no longer work (e.g. shielding, and coupling)

CIF Read/Write no longer supported.

The :select and select_q tcl functions are no longer supported.
These functions may be referenced in .tcl files located in the directory:
$MMI_TOOLS/../mmi_local/max.  Tcl files that reference these functions
should be removed, or modified to use new select functions.
To see new select functions, invoke "Text Commands/Variables" from
the Help menu, and search for "sel_".
Note: Micro Magic sometimes provided lvs and calibre scripts to customers
as tcl files that were installed in this directory.  Both lvs and calibre
support are now included inside max, and any such files in the
mmi_local directory should be removed.


Known Limitations
-----------------

Interactive DRC doesn't work for all angle or 45 degree geometries

Netlist extract doesn't work for all angle or 45 degree geometries

Select net doesn't work for all angle or 45 degree gates

Mask operations (i.e. bloats and shrinks) during GDS read/write don't 
	work on non-manhattan data.




